# Frontend Engineering Rule

- Use Next.js App Router and TypeScript strict mode.
- Use Server Components by default.
- Keep client boundaries small and intentional.
- Use `next/image` and provide meaningful alt text or empty alt for decorative images.
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation.
- Use route Metadata APIs and file-based metadata.
- Avoid waterfalls and fetch independent resources in parallel.
- Do not define components inside components.
- Keep nonprimitive default props outside render where appropriate.
- Use semantic HTML before ARIA.
- Use shadcn/ui primitives as owned source and customize them to the Hendricks design system.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and broad barrel imports.
- Prefer CSS transitions and transforms over JavaScript animation.
- Every animation must have a reduced-motion equivalent.
- Never render important page copy only after hydration.
